{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/691836-are-there-any-bloodline-npcs-in-any-vtr-books","id":691836,"title":"Are there any Bloodline NPCs in any VtR books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-06T18:21:02-07:00","id":691836,"title":"Are there any Bloodline NPCs in any VtR books?","content":"As far as I know, Natasha Preston (from the Core Rulebook) is the only NPC who is a member of a Bloodline. Does anyone know if there are any other Bloodline NPCs in any of the other books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8145-voidmaster","name":"VoidMaster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T18:34:36-07:00","id":691873,"title":"","content":"There's a few in Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners, at least one in Shadows of Mexico, a couple in Requiem for Rome's Fall of the Camarilla, a few in the Ancients books, Mysteries and Bloodlines. There's also more than a few in the clanbooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:38:15-07:00","id":692246,"title":"","content":"In general, you won't see an NPC with a Bloodline (or any other really special thing) unless that Bloodline or whatever is detailed within the core or the book the NPC is in. Standard operating procedure for nWoD books is to limit the amount of cross-referencing - the material should be totally usable with just the core and the book in question. They've played with it over the years but that's the general philosophy. <br /> <br /> So you'll find them in books that allocate space for both NPCs and that Bloodline. Clanbooks are a good example of books that list a couple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}